 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The output Y is the logical complement of input A: a LOW input gives a HIGH output and a HIGH input gives a LOW output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Internal structure",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "From A to Y the gate is three inverter stages in cascade."
  },
  {
   "topic": "AHC and AHCT",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 74AHC1G04 has CMOS input thresholds (VIH 3.85 V min, VIL 1.65 V max at VCC = 5.5 V) and works from 2.0 V to 5.5 V. The 74AHCT1G04 has TTL thresholds (VIH 2.0 V, VIL 0.8 V) and works from 4.5 V to 5.5 V. With its input held at 3.4 V and VCC = 5.5 V the 74AHCT1G04 draws an additional supply current ΔICC of up to 1.35 mA at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Overvoltage-tolerant input",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The input may be driven up to 5.5 V with any supply in range, which lets the gate work as a level translator between supply domains."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Output impedance is symmetrical between HIGH and LOW, and rising and falling delays are balanced."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input edge rate",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Maximum input rise and fall rate: 100 ns/V at VCC = 3.3 V ± 0.3 V and 20 ns/V at VCC = 5.0 V ± 0.5 V for the 74AHC1G04; 20 ns/V at VCC = 5.0 V ± 0.5 V for the 74AHCT1G04."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Robustness",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Latch-up current: over 100 mA (JESD 78, Class II, Level A). ESD: over 2000 V HBM, JS-001 class 2; over 1000 V CDM, JS-002 class C3."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching measurement",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Delays are timed between the VM crossings of input and output. For the 74AHC1G04 the input swings GND to VCC and both VM levels are half of VCC; for the 74AHCT1G04 the input swings GND to 3.0 V with VM 1.5 V, and the output VM is half of VCC. The load CL includes the jig and probe, and RT matches the generator's output impedance."
  }
 ],
